cal L_k=\\{S_0,\\dots ,S_{k-1}\\}\\cup\\{V_1,\\dots ,V_c\\}\n\\]\n\ncovers every point of \\(T_n\\).\n\n*Proof of covering.*\n\n*Left‑hand columns.*  \nIf \\((a,b)\\in T_n\\) satisfies \\(1\\le a\\le c\\), then the point lies on the vertical line \\(V_a\\).\n\n*Right‑hand columns.*  \nAssume \\(a>c\\).  Write \\(a=c+i\\) with \\(i\\in\\{1,\\dots ,k\\}\\); thus  \n\n\\[\na=n-k+i .\n\\]\n\nFrom the defining inequality \\(a+b\\le n+1\\) we obtain  \n\n\\[\nb\\le n+1-a = n+1-(c+i)=k+1-i .\n\\tag{4}\n\\]\n\nHence the admissible ordinates in column \\(a\\) are  \n\n\\[\n1\\le b\\le k+1-i .\n\\tag{5}\n\\]\n\nFor a point \\((a,b)=(c+i,b)\\) satisfying (5), set  \n\n\\[\nj:=i-b .\n\\tag{6}\n\\]\n\nBecause of (5) we have \\(0\\le j\\le i-1\\le k-1\\); consequently \\(j\\) is an integer between \\(0\\) and \\(k-1\\), so the line \\(S_j\\) belongs to \\(\\mathcal L_k\\).\n\nNow substitute \\(a=c+i\\) and \\(j=i-b\\) into the equation of \\(S_j\\):\n\n\\[\ny = x-(c+j)=x-(c+(i-b))=x-(c+i-b).\n\\]\n\nEvaluating at \\((x,y)=(a,b)=(c+i,b)\\) gives  \n\n\\[\nb = (c+i)-(c+i-b)=b ,\n\\]\n\nso \\((a,b)\\) indeed lies on \\(S_j\\).\n\nThus every point of \\(T_n\\) with \\(a>c\\) is covered by a sunny line, while the points with \\(a\\le c\\) are covered by a vertical line. ∎\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\n### Theorem (Complete description of admissible \\(k\\))\n\nFor a given integer \\(n\\ge 3\\) the set of non‑negative integers \\(k\\) for which there exist \\(n\\) distinct lines satisfying the covering condition and containing exactly \\(k\\) sunny lines is  \n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\{0,1,2,\\dots ,n\\}}.\n\\]\n\n*Proof.*  \nLemma 1 shows that \\(k=0\\) is attainable.  \nLemma 2 shows that for every \\(k\\) with \\(1\\le k\\le n\\) such a configuration exists.  \nSince we must use exactly \\(n\\) lines, the number of sunny lines cannot exceed \\(n\\); therefore no \\(k>n\\) is possible. ∎\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\n**Thus the admissible values of \\(k\\) are precisely all integers from \\(0\\) up to \\(n\\).**\n\n\n### Verification Task Reminder ###\n\nYour task is to act as an IMO grader. Now, generate the **summary** and the **step-by-step verification log** for the solution above. In your log, justify each correct step and explain in detail any errors or justification gaps you find, as specified in the instructions above.\n\n"
