a,b)\\in S_n\\) we have \\(1\\le b\\le n\\), hence \\((a,b)\\) lies on the line\n\\(y=b\\).  Thus the \\(n\\) lines \\(\\{\\ell_1,\\dots ,\\ell_n\\}\\) cover all points of\n\\(S_n\\) and contain **no** sunny line.\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\n#### 7.  Conclusion  \n\nA covering of the required type exists for every \\(n\\ge 3\\), but such a covering\ncannot contain any sunny line.  Consequently the only possible number of sunny\nlines is  \n\n\\[\n\\boxed{k=0}.\n\\]\n\n\n### Verification Task Reminder ###\n\nYour task is to act as an IMO grader. Now, generate the **summary** and the **step-by-step verification log** for the solution above. In your log, justify each correct step and explain in detail any errors or justification gaps you find, as specified in the instructions above.\n\n"
